      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Over-application of antibiotic ointment can sometimes lead to unintended consequences, such as skin irritation or the weakening of the skin's natural barrier, which could potentially increase the risk of infection. Importantly, wound healing requires some level of immune response and oxygen reaching the wound, which might be compromised if you cover the wound too tightly with gauze. A respectful and balanced approach is best. Wrap the wound loosely to keep it clean without inhibiting circulation and ensure the ointment is thoroughly but not excessively applied. If you notice redness, swelling, pain, or if the wound appears to be getting worse instead of better, then it is essential to visit a healthcare provider. The goal is to support healthy healing, not to mask symptoms that may require professional care.",
